.Dd November 5, 2026
.Dt PIDP11-INSTALL-SYSTEMS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pidp11-install-systems
.Nd download and install PDP-11 operating system disk images
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -force
.Op Fl -tarball Ar file
.Op Fl -email Ar address
.Op Ar
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
downloads PDP-11 operating system disk images into
.Pa /var/lib/pidp11/systems
and registers them in the front panel boot selections menu.
Run it as root
.Pq Xr sudo 8 ;
the installed files end up owned by the
.Ar pidp11
service account.
.Pp
The disk images are read-write and hold your work, so existing files are
never overwritten unless
.Fl -force
is given.
.Sh COMMANDS
With no command,
.Cm list
is the default.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm list
Show the systems installed and the boot selections.
.It Cm base
The standard set: Unix v6/v7, System III/V, RSX-11M+, 2.11BSD and
more (a 122 MB download, several GB installed).
.It Cm 211bsd+
Chase Covello's updated 2.11BSD (boot code 0211).
.It Cm rsx11bq
Johnny Billquist's RSX-11M+ with BQTC/IP (boot code 2024).
.It Cm all
.Cm base ,
.Cm 211bsd+
and
.Cm rsx11bq .
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -force
Overwrite files that already exist.
This destroys any changes made to the disk images!
.It Fl -tarball Ar file
Use an already downloaded
.Ar file
(a systems.tar.gz) for the
.Cm base
command instead of fetching it.
.It Fl -email Ar address
Email address for the anonymous FTP login used by
.Cm rsx11bq ,
a courtesy to the server's operator.
Default: none.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev PIDP11_SYSTEMSDIR
Install directory for the disk images.
Default:
.Pa /var/lib/pidp11/systems .
.It Ev PIDP11_DATADIR
Directory holding the boot selections file and boot scripts.
Default:
.Pa /usr/share/pidp11 .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Fetch everything and then show what is installed:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sudo pidp11-install-systems all
pidp11-install-systems list
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pdp11 1 ,
.Xr pidp11-sty 1
